      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Simplify $(P∨Q)∨(Q∨R).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the associative and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∨(Q∨R) & ≡((P∨Q)∨Q)∨R \\\\  & ≡(P∨(Q∨Q))∨R \\\\  & ≡(P∨Q)∨R.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
