      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Simplify $(A∨B)∨(C∨B).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the associative, commutative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∨B)∨(C∨B) & ≡(A∨B)∨(B∨C) \\\\  & ≡A∨(B∨B)∨C \\\\  & ≡A∨B∨C \\\\  & ≡A∨C∨B \\\\  & ≡(A∨C)∨B.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
