      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Simplify $(Q∧P)∧Q.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the commutative, associative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Q∧P)∧Q & ≡(P∧Q)∧Q \\\\  & ≡P∧(Q∧Q) \\\\  & ≡P∧Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
